      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let us examine the conversation line by line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Что же это такое?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What is this?' Here 'what' sets up the idea, while 'on earth' comes at the end for emphasis.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Что у вас за ресторан?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What kind of restaurant is this?' Russian leaves out 'am', 'is', or 'are' in the present tense, linking 'what' straight to 'restaurant'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Простите, я не хотела.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I'm sorry, I didn't mean to.' The '-a' on the end of the past-tense verb for 'wanted' tells you the subject is feminine. Chef Viktor answers straight away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Какие планы на вечер?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Any plans for tonight?' Russian leaves out 'am', 'is', or 'are' in the present tense, linking 'plans' straight to 'evening'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "У меня никаких.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I don't have any.' Notice the word order: 'me' comes first, and 'me' finishes the sentence.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "А что, есть варианты?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Got something in mind?' Elena starts with 'what' and pairs it with 'there is' to make the point clear. Then Chef Viktor replies.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Вариант один.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'One thing.' Chef Viktor puts 'option' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'one'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Но нужно быть вдвоём.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'But it takes two.' You'll hear 'necessary' all the time in the show, here connected with 'the two of us together'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Какой тонкий намёк.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What a subtle hint.' The question word for 'what a' comes right at the start, followed directly by 'hint'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Я хотела поехать за покупками.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I wanted to go shopping.' The key word here means 'I', which Elena combines with 'wanted'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "elena",
      "t": "Но твой вариант мне нравится.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'But I like your idea.' The first content word means 'option', and 'is pleasing' rounds out the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Отлично.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Excellent.' A compact expression built around 'perfect' and 'perfect'. Now let us listen to the conversation once again.",
      "gap": 0.9
